{{Wireless adapter |brand=Silex |model=SX-SDCAG |revision= |upc= |ean= |asin= |price= |est_release_date= |fcc_date=04/13/2010 |manuf_country=Japan |manuf= |manuf_model= |manuf_rev= |if=SDIO (SD) |vendor_id= |device_id= |subvendor_id= |subdevice_id= |fcc_id=N6C-SXSDCAG |ic_id=4908B-SXSDCAG |chip1_brand=Atheros |chip1_model=AR6002 |chip2_brand= |chip2_model= |chip3_brand= |chip3_model= |flags= |ant_conn=U.FL |802dot11_protocols=abg |txchains= |rxchains= |sstreams= |oui= |lin_driver= |win_driver= }} {{TagLine|SX-SDCAG 802.11a/b/g SDIO Module}}
"silex technology", "PCA 128-00197-100 Rev X2", "PX10450XA", and "PW06800AX" is silkscreened on the board in the FCC photos. The device appears to be using a '''Mitsumi''' module.
Per the FCC manual, this device is using AR6002XZ (CSP AR6002).
